From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: start the HTT tx completion with no msdu

Since the bitmap tx pool, ath11k_dp_tx_htt_tx_complete_buf() only
assigns msdu when the completion's id is in the pool, but the "unknown
msdu_id" check right after reads it either way: a completion for an id
that is not pending - a duplicate, or one that races the ring cleanup -
went on with whatever was on the stack and dereferenced it. The other
two completion paths already start from NULL.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -402,7 +402,7 @@ ath11k_dp_tx_htt_tx_complete_buf(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 				 struct ath11k_dp_htt_wbm_tx_status *ts)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_tx_status status = {};
-	struct sk_buff *msdu;
+	struct sk_buff *msdu = NULL;
 	struct ieee80211_tx_info *info;
 	struct ath11k_skb_cb *skb_cb;
 	struct ath11k *ar;
